 * <p>Because the household is keyed on {@code (lastName, postcode)} (see
 * {@link Owner#householdId(String, String)}), owners sharing a last name and postcode are the
 * same household. Members of the same household are allowed to coexist as long as they have
 * distinct identities (a different normalized telephone, enforced by
 * {@link #assertIdentityIsUnique(Owner)}); an undeclared household member sharing an existing
 * household is still created but flagged as a possible (suspected) duplicate, whereas a declared
 * household member ({@code sharesHousehold} set) is left unflagged. Allowing household members to
 * coexist is what lets the household membership-level ceiling (see
 * {@link #computeMembershipLevel(Owner)}) compare a new owner against the existing members.
 */
@Override
@Transactional
public void saveOwner(Owner owner, boolean sharesHousehold) throws DataAccessException {
    boolean isCreate = owner.isNew();
    assertEmailDomainAllowed(owner);
    assertIdentityIsUnique(owner);
    if (owner.isNew()) {
        assertCityHasCapacity(owner);
    }

